Notebook[
 {Cell[CellGroupData[
    {Cell["Four-Derivative Corrections to the Three-Charge BMPV Black Hole", 
      "Title", ExpressionUUID -> "e8ce9e06-1b88-4c70-aa4d-66f8399f8b58"], 
     Cell["Version-3 human notation guide. The archived equation and source Input cells are unchanged; the independent convention guard added below does not modify them. In the compact solution and verifier notebooks: x=r^2; q1,q2,q3 \
are the harmonic parameters mu1,mu2,mu3, not normalized conserved charges; \
jrot is the rotation parameter j; U1,U2,U3 are the electric corrections delta \
u_I; B1,B2,B3 are the gauge-covariant fibre corrections; Om is delta omega; \
Ft, Gr, and Sq are the temporal warp, radial warp, and squashing corrections; \
P and S are delta p and delta s, where X1=exp(2p/3-s), X2=exp(2p/3+s), and \
X3=exp(-4p/3). Physical quantities are Q_I=Pi mu_I/(4 G5) and J1=J2=Pi j/(4 \
G5). See the report section 'Human-readable notation and result at a glance' \
for the full dictionary.", "Text"], Cell["Package provenance. This is the \
root construction notebook for the O(j) verification chain. Optional \
project-path and cache-writing cells were removed; every definition needed by \
the derivation is contained here. No external file is read when it is \
evaluated.", "Text", ExpressionUUID -> 
       "a234a4df-2b5e-46dc-825e-697c7cba9c4a"], 
     Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Ungauged five-dimensional STU model in the \
Riemann field-redefinition frame", "Subtitle", ExpressionUUID -> 
          "09140e0b-066c-4d11-bb5e-be6cbccfb8f6"], Cell["Purpose. This \
notebook combines the rotating BMPV ansatz with the complete \
Riemann-containing standard-Weyl STU invariant. It keeps the three gauge \
potentials general until the two-derivative BMPV background is imposed. The \
calculation is organized as a first-order problem: the two-derivative \
linearized operator acts on unknown corrections, while the four-derivative \
invariant supplies a fixed source evaluated on the zeroth-order BMPV \
background.", "Text", ExpressionUUID -> 
          "6ad7bcb4-4963-4cbe-937b-3727dc7043ba"], Cell["Conventions. \
Coordinates are {t,r,theta,phi,psi}, eta = d psi + cos(theta) d phi, and the \
metric signature is mostly plus. The coupling vector lam = {lam1,lam2,lam3} \
labels the three standard-Weyl STU gravity invariants. This is an ungauged \
calculation: the AdS gauge coupling is set to zero from the beginning.", 
         "Text", ExpressionUUID -> "687d7cdf-0cae-4055-9b11-02f03a5dbd1f"], 
        Cell["Levi--Civita and chart orientation. In the oriented orthonormal frame, the flat-index symbol has epsilonLower[0,1,2,3,4]=+1 and epsilonUpper[0,1,2,3,4]=-1. The curved tensor is obtained with five vielbeins and includes their determinant. The BMPV base orientation is vol4=-(r^3/8) dr wedge sigma1 wedge sigma2 wedge sigma3, so the coordinate order (t,r,theta,phi,psi) reverses the physical orientation. Hence the curved components are epsilonLower[trthetaphipsi]=-Sqrt[-g] and epsilonUpper[trthetaphipsi]=+1/Sqrt[-g]. The historical epsSymbol=Normal[LeviCivitaTensor[5]] is the positive alternating coordinate density epsilonTilde=Sqrt[-g] epsilonUpper, exactly as required by the component action. No gauge-potential sign is reversed.", "Text"],
        Cell[BoxData["alternatingCoordinateDensity=Normal[LeviCivitaTensor[5]]; frameEpsilonLowerOrdered=+1; frameEpsilonUpperOrdered=-1; coordinateOrientationSign=-1; coordinateEpsilonLowerSign=-1; coordinateEpsilonUpperSign=+1; actionArrayOrdered=alternatingCoordinateDensity[[1,2,3,4,5]]; leviCivitaConventionPass=TrueQ[{frameEpsilonLowerOrdered,frameEpsilonUpperOrdered,coordinateOrientationSign,coordinateEpsilonLowerSign,coordinateEpsilonUpperSign,actionArrayOrdered}=={1,-1,-1,-1,1,1}]; Print[<|\"FlatSymbolLower01234\"->frameEpsilonLowerOrdered,\"FlatSymbolUpper01234\"->frameEpsilonUpperOrdered,\"CurvedCoordinateLowerSign\"->coordinateEpsilonLowerSign,\"CurvedCoordinateUpperSign\"->coordinateEpsilonUpperSign,\"AlternatingDensity\"->actionArrayOrdered,\"Pass\"->leviCivitaConventionPass|>];"], "Input"],
        Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["1. Kernel setup and project paths", 
            "Section", ExpressionUUID -> 
             "ad8781b4-df7a-426b-a1a7-bb61fa6dda8d"], 
           Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "\"Global`*\"", 
                 "]"}], ";", RowBox[{"$RecursionLimit", "=", "100000"}], ";", 
               RowBox[{"$MaxExtraPrecision", "=", "10000"}], ";", RowBox[
                {"dim", "=", "5"}], ";", RowBox[{"coords", "=", 
                 RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"t", ",", "r", ",", "theta", ",", 
                     "phi", ",", "psi"}], "}"}]}], ";", RowBox[{"indexRange", 
                 "=", RowBox[{"Range", "[", "dim", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input", 
            CellLabel -> "In[27]:=", ExpressionUUID -> 
             "320dfca3-6d10-4ec4-b21e-840949a6083e"]}, Open]], 
        Cell[CellGroupData[
          {Cell["2. General rotating cohomogeneity-one ansatz", "Section", 
            ExpressionUUID -> "a906ec1c-ae37-474b-ab7c-96aa0dc36bc4"], 
           Cell["The Hopf-fibre components vI(r) are independent of the \
electric potentials uI(r). This is more general than imposing A^I = uI (dt + \
omega eta) before variation and prevents the ansatz from deleting possible \
four-derivative gauge corrections.", "Text", ExpressionUUID -> 
             "b413042f-d341-44a7-a941-eae601449089"], 
           Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"dtCov", "=", RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"1", ",", "0", ",", "0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], 
                   "}"}]}], ";", RowBox[{"drCov", "=", RowBox[{"{", 
                   RowBox[{"0", ",", "1", ",", "0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], 
                   "}"}]}], ";", RowBox[{"dThetaCov", "=", RowBox[
                  {"{", RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "1", ",", "0", ",", 
                     "0"}], "}"}]}], ";", RowBox[{"dPhiCov", "=", 
                 RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0", ",", "1", ",", 
                     "0"}], "}"}]}], ";", RowBox[{"etaCov", "=", 
                 RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0", ",", 
                     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "theta", "]"}], ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], 
               ";", RowBox[{"ThetaCov", "=", RowBox[{"dtCov", "+", 
                   RowBox[{RowBox[{"omega", "[", "r", "]"}], " ", 
                     "etaCov"}]}]}], ";", RowBox[{"gdd", "=", RowBox[
                  {"Simplify", "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", RowBox[
                          {"Exp", "[", RowBox[{"2", " ", RowBox[{"f", "[", 
                          "r", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
                         RowBox[{"Times", ",", "ThetaCov", ",", "ThetaCov"}], 
                         "]"}]}], "+", RowBox[{RowBox[{"Exp", "[", RowBox[
                          {"2", " ", RowBox[{"gr", "[", "r", "]"}]}], "]"}], 
                       " ", RowBox[{"Outer", "[", RowBox[{"Times", ",", 
                          "drCov", ",", "drCov"}], "]"}]}], "+", RowBox[
                      {FractionBox["1", "4"], " ", RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
                         RowBox[{"2", " ", RowBox[{"hr", "[", "r", "]"}]}], 
                         "]"}], " ", SuperscriptBox["r", "2"], " ", RowBox[
                        {"(", RowBox[{RowBox[{"Outer", "[", RowBox[{"Times", 
                          ",", "dThetaCov", ",", "dThetaCov"}], "]"}], "+", 
                          RowBox[{SuperscriptBox[RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "theta", 
                          "]"}], "2"], " ", RowBox[{"Outer", "[", RowBox[
                          {"Times", ",", "dPhiCov", ",", "dPhiCov"}], 
                          "]"}]}], "+", RowBox[{RowBox[{"Exp", "[", RowBox[
                          {"2", " ", RowBox[{"squ", "[", "r", "]"}]}], "]"}], 
                          " ", RowBox[{"Outer", "[", RowBox[{"Times", ",", 
                          "etaCov", ",", "etaCov"}], "]"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}], 
                   "]"}]}], ";", RowBox[{"guu", "=", RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
                   TemplateBox[{"gdd"}, "Inverse"], "]"}]}], ";", RowBox[
                {"sdetg", "=", RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", RowBox[
                    {"PowerExpand", "[", SqrtBox[RowBox[{"-", RowBox[{"Det", 
                          "[", "gdd", "]"}]}]], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], 
            "Input", InitializationCell -> False, CellLabel -> "In[28]:=", 
            ExpressionUUID -> "116932aa-6544-4e1a-841c-5818160817e9"], 
           Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[
